jamie_sales: Hi all  Mike at BeaconMart wants a 90-day pilot: streaming responses that may trigger function/tool calls and must return strictly validated JSON per tenant. They also asked for SAML SSO, KMS/BYOK options, a one-page infra runbook for ephemeral tokens, and a pricing estimate for ~5M tokens/day (peak ~50 rps). Can SEs outline steps + blockers?
mike_cust: we need a runnable SDK example (websocket) we can drop into our staging infra, plus guidance on token rotation and backpressure. Low ops surface preferred.
oscar_se: Summary plan: start with Hosted demo to move fast. If BeaconMart needs isolation or guaranteed tail latency we propose Dedicated trial. For the SDK well show websocket streaming + function_call lifecycle + schema validation.
oscar_se: POC checklist: 1) JSON schemas for each function (we support JSON Schema draft-2020-12), 2) SAML IdP metadata, 3) KMS intent (BYOK vs Redwood-managed), 4) latency p95 target, 5) any data-residency constraints.
lina_prod: Security quick answers to include in sales replies: TLS 1.3 in transit, AES-256 at rest, customer KMS via BYOK supported in Private/Dedicated, configurable audit-log retention, SOC2 summary available. I'll attach the short Q&A doc link.
sec_bot: Security answers uploaded: https://redwood.internal/sq/beacon-3187654321 (sales+security) :lock:
raj_infra: Streaming + handshake notes: prefer WebSocket for low latency; use ephemeral tokens issued by customer auth bridge or our token-service. Recommended TTL ~1h for POC; rotate preemptively every 40-50m by reconnecting. Avoid in-stream token swaps. For backpressure use client-side smoothing and server continuous-batching.
raj_infra: Handshake example (ephemeral token flow):
```bash
# request ephemeral token from your auth bridge
curl -X POST https://auth.beacon.example/api/ephemeral -d '{"svc":"beacon-poc"}' | jq -r .token
# connect to Redwood stream
wscat -c "wss://stream.redwood.ai/v1/chat?token=<EPHEMERAL>"
```
raj_infra: Rotation strategy: request new token on a background timer (every 40m), then open a new socket and gracefully swap with a short drain window. Don't rotate mid-request.
oscar_se: SDK example (node) we'll hand off so infra can copy/paste quickly:```js
const Redwood = require('redwood-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const ws = client.stream({ model: 'redwood-chat-1', structured_output: true, schema: {/* JSON schema */} });
ws.send({ input: 'Get pending refunds for tenant=99', functions: [{ name: 'get_refunds', schema: { type: 'object', properties: { tenant_id: { type: 'integer' } } } }] });
ws.on('message', async (ev) => {
  if (ev.type === 'function_call') {
    const res = await callLocalService(ev.args);
    ws.send({ function_response: res });
  } else if (ev.type === 'chunk') {
    process.stdout.write(ev.text);
  }
});
```
oscar_se: Also provide a tiny test harness that runs sample prompts against the model and asserts JSON schema conformance before handing results to downstream services.
lina_prod: Pricing guidance for sales: propose two paths — (A) Hosted pilot with a blended pilot rate + capped spend for 90d; (B) Dedicated trial with a monthly commit and lower per-token unit cost. I'll prepare a short table with ballpark numbers for both.
oscar_se: Enterprise blocker to call out: if BeaconMart insists that PII must remain on-prem we need to plan a Private deployment (~6-8 weeks). If PII can stay in cloud but under BYOK and VPC egress, Hosted + BYOK can work for pilot.
jamie_sales: Mike  can you share SAML metadata and confirm whether any tenant data needs to be processed on-prem for the pilot? Also propose 90m demo slot next Wed 9am PT.
mike_cust: SAML metadata will be sent today. No on-prem PII for pilot. Wed 9am PT works; I'll invite infra.
ops_bot: Demo environment provisioned: demo-beacon-3187654321  provisioned resources + ephemeral token bridge enabled. Creds will be DMed to participants.
sec_bot: Note: if they request SOC2 artifacts copy, run appendix A.3 before demo.
oscar_se: Action items: I'll post the Node SDK example + a small schema test harness; Raj will upload the one-page runbook (handshake, rotation, failure modes); Lina will attach security artifacts and the pricing ballpark; Jamie will collect SAML metadata and send calendar invite.
jamie_sales: Great, let's aim to have artifacts in thread by EOD so BeaconMart can prep. Thanks team!
